# Create the reference graphic

Importing `{{packageName}}` registers `{{referenceActionName}}()` on ggaction's
complete chart program.

```javascript
import { chart } from "ggaction";
import { renderToSVG } from "ggaction/svg";
import "{{packageName}}";

const program = chart()
  .createCanvas({ width: 160, height: 120 })
  .{{referenceActionName}}();

const svg = renderToSVG(program);
```

The result is one blue circle. Customize `id`, `x`, `y`, `radius`, or `fill`
without introducing a renderer owned by the extension.

The executable source is
[examples/reference/program.js]({{ site.repository_url }}/blob/main/examples/reference/program.js),
and the normative behavior is
[REF]({{ site.repository_url }}/blob/main/spec/features/reference.md).
